{"name":"Sweet Taffy","hex":"#ecbcd4","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting of sugars.","Retaining a portion of sugar."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Used as a positive response to good news or information."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet"},{"term":"taffy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A soft, chewy candy made from boiled sugar, molasses, or corn syrup and butter.","Flattery."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/taffy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Taffy (candy)","blocks":[{"text":"Taffy is a type of candy invented in the United States, made by stretching or pulling a sticky mass of a soft candy base, made of boiled sugar, butter, vegetable oil, flavorings, and colorings, until it becomes aerated, resulting in a light, fluffy and chewy candy. When this process is complete, the taffy is rolled, cut into small pieces and wrapped in wax paper to keep it soft. It is usually pastel-colored and fruit-flavored, but other flavors are common as well, including molasses and the \"classic\" (unflavored) taffy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Salt_water_taffy.jpg/330px-Salt_water_taffy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taffy_(candy)"},{"title":"Taffy (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Taffy is a French animated television series co-created by Mike de Sève and Pierre Sissman. The series is produced by Cyber Group Studios, in co-production with Turner Broadcasting System Europe with the participation of France 4 for the first season and WarnerMedia and Gulli for the second season. The series airs on Boomerang all across Europe. In September 2019, the series was renewed for a second season. On March 30, 2022, Cyber Group Studios and Gulli renewed the series for a third season."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/17/Taffy%28TVseries%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taffy_(TV_series)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Salt_water_taffy.jpg/500px-Salt_water_taffy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Salt_water_taffy.jpg/1280px-Salt_water_taffy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Salt_water_taffy.jpg/500px-Salt_water_taffy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASalt_water_taffy.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/The_Taffy_Shop%2C_Estes_Park_%282024%29-104A4619.jpg/500px-The_Taffy_Shop%2C_Estes_Park_%282024%29-104A4619.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/The_Taffy_Shop%2C_Estes_Park_%282024%29-104A4619.jpg/1280px-The_Taffy_Shop%2C_Estes_Park_%282024%29-104A4619.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/The_Taffy_Shop%2C_Estes_Park_%282024%29-104A4619.jpg/500px-The_Taffy_Shop%2C_Estes_Park_%282024%29-104A4619.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Salt water taffy production on an old Model K kiss-wrapping machine at the Taffy Shop (established in 1935) in Estes Park, Colorado","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Taffy_Shop%2C_Estes_Park_(2024)-104A4619.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Taffy_shop_at_San_Francisco_Pier_39%2C_October_2015_%2823162359765%29.jpg/500px-Taffy_shop_at_San_Francisco_Pier_39%2C_October_2015_%2823162359765%